  ]
 },
 "ambiguities": [
  {
   "id": "ecc-truncation-vs-mantissa-rounding",
   "text": "CelesTrak's TLE rendering truncates eccentricity to 7 digits but rounds (half up) BSTAR and the second derivative to a 5-digit mantissa (304/304 CelesTrak records reproduced with these rules; 0 with the opposite rules). No document states either rule; treat as observed CelesTrak behaviour. It is not universal: in the owner's Space-Track verification run (D-070) Space-Track's TLE for the same epoch differed from the CelesTrak-rendered line in the last one or two eccentricity digits (columns 32-33), consistent with rounding, and wrote a zero second derivative as 00000-0 (column 51) where CelesTrak writes 00000+0."
  },
  {
   "id": "mmdot-convention",
   "text": "CCSDS 4.2.4.7 NOTE 2 says TLE-sourced MEAN_MOTION_DOT/DDOT 'need to be divided by 2 and 6 respectively' but does not say which convention the OMM value carries. Observed: CelesTrak's OMM values equal the TLE fields as printed (301/301 records), i.e. the halved / sixth-ed values. Parsers converting to true derivatives must multiply by 2 and 6."
  }
 ],
